# The built proxy artifacts are 6 MiB each and are deliberately NOT committed:
# a binary blob in a diff is reviewed by nobody. What IS committed is
# ../provenance.json -- version, toolchain, build flags and a SHA-256 per
# architecture, which is 30 lines a person can actually read -- and
# scripts/build-egress-proxy.sh is what proves the bytes still match it.
#
# This rule lives here rather than relying on the repository's generic `bin/`
# rule on purpose: an ignore that happens to catch these files is one that
# stops catching them the day somebody narrows it, and 13 MiB of binaries
# would then become committable by accident.
ao-egress-proxy-linux-*
